      "source_text": "After an incredibly meaningful chapter, I’m excited to share that I’ve started a new journey in my career. I recently wrapped up my time at Southwest Airlines , where I had the privilege of working as an Aircraft Cybersecurity Engineer, and I’ve officially started a new position at Lockheed Martin MFC as a Cyber Systems Security Engineer, Sr. Leaving Southwest is definitely bittersweet. I’m grateful for the opportunity, trust, and confidence I was given during my time there. I learned a tremendous amount, grew both personally and professionally, and had the opportunity to work alongside some incredibly talented people. What I’ll remember most is the people and the culture. Southwest has a truly unique culture, and being part of it was an experience I’ll carry with me throughout my career. The relationships, challenges, and experiences I gained along the way have shaped me in ways I’ll continue to appreciate. Now, I’m incredibly excited about what’s ahead at Lockheed Martin. I’m looking forward to taking on new challenges, learning new technologies and approaches, and continuing to grow in an area I’m passionate about — aerospace and aviation cybersecurity. I’m excited to see where this next chapter takes me and to continue connecting with others who are passionate about cybersecurity, aviation, aerospace, and protecting the systems that keep our world moving. Here’s to new challenges, continued growth, and the opportunity to make an impact in a new arena. Onward and upward! #Cybersecurity #Aerospace #Aviation #CyberSecurity #LockheedMartin #CareerGrowth",
